  "verbalization": "Myricetin-3-O-Beta-D-Glucuronide appears to exert its biological effects through multiple pathways, with a central role in targeting UDP-glucuronosyltransferase 1A4 and phosphatidylinositol 4-kinase type 2-beta. These targets are implicated in the regulation of cellular processes that may influence the behavior of SMMC-7721, a human liver cancer cell line. The observed relationship between Myricetin-3-O-Beta-D-Glucuronide and SMMC-7721 is likely mediated through these molecular interactions, which could modulate signaling pathways or metabolic processes that contribute to the cell's proliferation or survival. The integration of these targets suggests a potential mechanism by which the compound may exert its anti-cancer effects, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
